("api/on-click" :names ("on-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :CLICK snapshots with no payload. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :position 220927)
("api/on-selection" :names ("on-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :SELECTION snapshots with selected index or NIL. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached. ABI38 LIST-BOX specialization manages its convenience :LISTBOX-SELECTION observer; generic bindings remain separately managed. Selection snapshots include cached native event text/index." :position 222765)
("api/on-text-change" :names ("on-text-change") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TEXT-CHANGE snapshots with copied text. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :position 224995)
("api/on-toggle" :names ("on-toggle") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TOGGLE snapshots with boolean state. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :position 226820)
("api/owned-event" :names ("owned-event") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed CLOS construction supports subclasses, slot initargs, defaults and AFTER hooks. Native origin is NIL. Mixed ancestry with EVENT-HANDLER/window is invalid. Explicit destruction or session cleanup owns deletion; there is no GC finalizer." :position 228613)
("api/panel" :names ("panel") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for a child wxPanel." :position 230768)
("api/pending-events-p" :names ("pending-events-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxAppConsole::HasPendingEvents across the current application. Does not report OS input, idle work or timers that have not queued an event. It is an observation, not a guarantee about the next dispatch. Safe to query during callbacks." :position 231833)
("api/pop-event-handler" :names ("pop-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Detach the top entry. Default preserves native owned registry/root; DELETE true releases bridge ownership before native PopEventHandler deletion and clears canonical roots/bindings. Empty stacks reject instead of invoking native assertions." :position 232941)
("api/post-event" :names ("post-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post an independent detached copy with wxPostEvent/AddPendingEvent; attach the receiver as copy origin. Input stays live/unchanged and may be destroyed or changed immediately. Delivery is asynchronous in the managed GUI session." :position 234360)
("api/previous-handler" :names ("previous-handler" "(setf previous-handler)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the native previous link. SETF mirrors NEXT-HANDLER, joining vacant source-previous/peer-next endpoints reciprocally or detaching one edge for NIL. Self/cycle/conflicting occupied endpoints reject before mutation; an existing reciprocal pair is idempotent." :position 235978)
("api/process-event" :names ("process-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously dispatch a fresh owned synthetic event through ProcessEvent, copy final veto state and then delete the event. Observer callbacks may run while handled-p is NIL because they Skip; native consumption/default handling determines the first result. Final veto is independent of handled-p and may be true from initial VETOED-P even without a matching handler. Close dispatch can run frame defaults. Callback errors re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary; handled nested errors do not stop RUN. No final values are returned when a condition escapes, and earlier callback mutations are not rolled back. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :position 238123)
("api/process-event-locally" :names ("process-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously process an independent detached copy with ProcessEventLocally, including local pre-processing and native chained handlers, without normal outer global-filter/parent/application fallback. Source remains live/unchanged. Observer delivery can return handled NIL; final veto is independent. Native local static/default handlers may still execute, including frame-close behavior; local processing is not observer-only or a no-default-action mode." :position 242556)
("api/process-events" :names ("process-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Yield to GUI events and process idle work without waiting for new input; re-signal callback errors after returning from native polling." :position 244754)
("api/process-pending-events" :names ("process-pending-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Dispatch queued wx events for all pending handlers of the bridge application via ProcessPendingEvents. Does not yield to OS input or run ProcessIdle. Does not wait for new events; callback duration and continuously requeued work may delay return. Callback conditions are contained at the native boundary and re-signaled afterwards." :position 245760)
("api/process-window-event" :names ("process-window-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Process a detached copy through native GetEventHandler stack routing, window and normal parent/application fallback. Source remains alive/unchanged; copy origin is WINDOW and callback source can be a pushed handler. Callback conditions re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary." :position 247395)
("api/process-window-event-locally" :names ("process-window-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Search the window and its pushed handlers with local pre-processing/validators, without normal upward window propagation. Process an independent detached copy with receiver-window origin and unchanged source. Observer delivery may still return handled NIL. Native local static/default handlers can still run, including frame-close behavior; local routing is not observer-only." :position 248802)
("api/pulse-gauge" :names ("pulse-gauge") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request platform-native indeterminate progress. Call periodically while keeping the GUI event loop responsive. Visual animation and value readings vary by platform; no timer, worker dispatch or completion event is provided. SETF GAUGE-VALUE restores determinate mode." :position 250425)
("api/push-event-handler" :names ("push-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Push above the existing stack top while keeping native ownership in the bridge registry. Reject linked/attached or borrowed window/app peers, active session bindings and queued session events before mutation." :position 251712)
("api/queue-click" :names ("queue-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post a button click for later dispatch. It uses the handler registered at dispatch time, including any replacement." :position 253037)
("api/queue-event" :names ("queue-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Queue a copied synthetic event: wxCommandEvent for seven command kinds, wxCloseEvent for close/session kinds and wxIdleEvent for :IDLE. Ordinary control properties are not changed directly. A queued close on a frame may run its native default closing action; use CLOSE-WINDOW for a synchronous acceptance result. Explicit UTF-8 lengths preserve text. Close events take no command payload, may be vetoable or non-vetoable, and do not normally propagate to parents. Registry types create wxCommandEvent or wxNotifyEvent according to their declared family. Initial veto applies only to custom notify types. Queuing offers no final veto/handled result; use PROCESS-EVENT when a synchronous decision is required. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :position 254012)
("api/realize-toolbar" :names ("realize-toolbar") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR with at least one tool or separator." :position 259002)
("api/register-event-type" :names ("register-event-type") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Allocate a process-local native event type and map NAME in the active session. Duplicate names, built-ins and unsupported families are rejected before registration. Names cannot be unregistered or replaced during this session. Registrations are session-wide metadata, not rolled back when an unrelated resource initializer fails. Native type IDs are not stable across processes." :position 259929)
("api/remove-event-handler" :names ("remove-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Preflight membership and detach without deletion. A live detached handler or handler belonging to another window returns NIL unchanged; only present entries reach native RemoveEventHandler, avoiding its absent-entry assertion." :position 261671)
("api/replace-text" :names ("replace-text") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace half-open native [FROM,TO) with VALUE using native Replace and text-change notification. Equal endpoints insert, empty VALUE removes. Mutation may precede a callback condition rethrow; handled conditions permit recovery. Exact no-op event counts, caret/selection and undo effects are port-specific." :position 263064)
("api/resume-event-propagation" :names ("resume-event-propagation") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Restore the native propagation level without changing Skip. Zero is allowed and keeps propagation stopped. Invalid LEVEL signals TYPE-ERROR; expired contexts reject native access." :position 264517)
("api/return-to-application-repl" :names ("return-to-application-repl") :kind :restart :kind-name "Restart" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Abandon the failing REPL evaluation or callback operation using the active debugger restart." :position 266281)
("api/run" :names ("run") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Block until STOP or the last top-level frame closes. Callback errors are re-signaled after returning from native code." :position 267092)
("api/selection" :names ("selection" "(setf selection)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read current selection: an index for CHOICE/LIST-BOX/NOTEBOOK, or a canonical managed TREE-ITEM view for TREE-CONTROL, with NIL when no selection exists. Reader NOTIFY is ignored. Writes are silent by default; notifying choice/list writes emit synthetic events, while notebook/tree writes use native vetoable selection. Return of a requested assignment does not prove native acceptance. Populated tree writes require a live same-tree item; NIL is empty-tree no-op only. Root creation and structural edits silently normalize valid selection before idle." :position 268003)
("api/show-modal" :names ("show-modal") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Run the native modal loop. Supported from menu/event callbacks, RUN or a pump; nested public SHOW-MODAL calls reject. Outer event contexts suspend during the modal call and become usable again after it returns; callbacks entered by the modal loop have their own valid innermost contexts. Bare callback errors cancel the modal operation and re-signal the primary condition after unwind. A nested notifying operation whose condition is handled locally can recover without cancelling. Manual RUN/pump/finish and structural menu edits remain guarded. Native close of the current dialog is consumed and cancels it; ancestor close events are consumed while modal. Public CLOSE-WINDOW on a protected ancestor rejects. Generic file UI prompts are redirected to guarded generic message dialogs. Internal prompts suspend borrowed contexts; errors or public cancellation unwind internal-to-outer sequentially. Cancelling an inner prompt normally returns to the outer dialog. Nested public SHOW-MODAL remains forbidden." :position 271021)
("api/show-window" :names ("show-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Show with true SHOW, hide with NIL. Existing one-argument calls still show the window and return it as their primary value." :position 274395)
("api/shown-p" :names ("shown-p" "(setf shown-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the window's own shown flag. A hidden ancestor does not change this flag; it does not report effective screen visibility." :position 275669)
("api/single-choice-dialog" :names ("single-choice-dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Construct a modal-only native single-choice dialog. Selection is always an in-range nonnegative index; NIL is not a choice. Strings are Unicode without NUL; empty strings are accepted. Defaults/subclass slot initargs and AFTER hooks use the native-backed CLOS protocol. Failed managed initialization destroys newly created resources; it does not reverse arbitrary external mutations." :position 277052)
("api/split-window" :names ("split-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER FIRST SECOND: attach distinct fully initialized panel children once, outside RUN/pumps/callbacks. Returns T." :position 279726)
("api/splitter-minimum-pane-size" :names ("splitter-minimum-pane-size" "(setf splitter-minimum-pane-size)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: positive pixel minimum; generic SETF accepts 1..536870911, returns supplied value." :position 280929)
("api/splitter-orientation" :names ("splitter-orientation") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: immutable :vertical (left/right) or :horizontal (top/bottom)." :position 282158)
("api/splitter-pane" :names ("splitter-pane") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER INDEX (0 or 1): canonical panel wrapper, or NIL before attachment." :position 283080)
("api/splitter-sash-gravity" :names ("splitter-sash-gravity" "(setf splitter-sash-gravity)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: native double gravity; generic SETF accepts real [0,1], returns supplied value." :position 283999)
("api/splitter-sash-position" :names ("splitter-sash-position" "(setf splitter-sash-position)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: native pixel position; generic SETF accepts 0..536870911, returns supplied value. Native centering/clamping/deferred geometry applies." :position 285191)
("api/splitter-split-p" :names ("splitter-split-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SPLITTER: boolean native split state." :position 286608)
("api/splitter-window" :names ("splitter-window") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed fixed two-panel window; :parent, :orientation, :sash-position, :minimum-pane-size and :sash-gravity initargs." :position 287416)
("api/status-bar" :names ("status-bar") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Concrete frame-owned status bar with :fields 1..16 (default 1)." :position 288712)
("api/status-field-count" :names ("status-field-count") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "STATUS-BAR." :position 289734)
("api/status-text" :names ("status-text" "(setf status-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "STATUS-BAR and optional zero-based FIELD (default 0)." :position 290395)
("api/stop" :names ("stop") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Leave RUN or end the application REPL. Stopping the loop does not destroy windows." :position 291590)
("api/stop-event-propagation" :names ("stop-event-propagation") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Set propagation level to zero. It does not set Skip; set Skip true when other local observers should continue without propagating to parents. Save the returned level for RESUME-EVENT-PROPAGATION." :position 292237)
("api/text" :names ("text" "(setf text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the current UTF-8 text; returned storage survives later native calls. ABI36 carries explicit UTF-8 lengths and rejects embedded NUL on writes; multiline native values use LF-separated lines. Read-only controls still allow programmatic edits. Native positions are not Lisp string indices." :position 293970)
("api/text-control" :names ("text-control") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for wxTextCtrl with text-change handler support." :position 295862)
("api/text-editable-p" :names ("text-editable-p" "(setf text-editable-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read whether native user editing is enabled. Programmatic text writes remain allowed." :position 297183)
("api/text-entry-dialog" :names ("text-entry-dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Construct a modal-only native text-entry dialog. Dialog value is native stored value, not a promise of live edit-buffer contents. Strings are Unicode without NUL; empty strings are accepted. Defaults/subclass slot initargs and AFTER hooks use the native-backed CLOS protocol. Failed managed initialization destroys newly created resources; it does not reverse arbitrary external mutations." :position 298299)
("api/text-insertion-point" :names ("text-insertion-point" "(setf text-insertion-point)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the native insertion offset." :position 300941)
("api/text-last-position" :names ("text-last-position") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the native end offset for use with native selection/editing operations." :position 302027)
("api/text-multiline-p" :names ("text-multiline-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the multiline style chosen at construction; no SETF." :position 302961)
("api/text-selection" :names ("text-selection" "(setf text-selection)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read two native selection offsets for current content." :position 303823)
("api/tool-checked-p" :names ("tool-checked-p" "(setf tool-checked-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR ID for a known check tool." :position 304960)
("api/tool-enabled-p" :names ("tool-enabled-p" "(setf tool-enabled-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR ID for a known action tool." :position 305991)
("api/toolbar" :names ("toolbar") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Concrete horizontal frame-owned toolbar window." :position 306955)
("api/toolbar-tool-count" :names ("toolbar-tool-count") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR." :position 307891)
("api/transfer-event" :names ("transfer-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Validate before consuming, then remove the actual event from the owned registry, attach receiver origin and hand it to wxQueueEvent. Input becomes non-live and cannot be accessed, cloned or destroyed by its former owner. Destination deletion or pending-event cancellation does not restore it." :position 308526)
("api/tree-control" :names ("tree-control") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Managed item tokens and canonical views, native selection/veto and bounded structural navigation." :position 310387)
("api/tree-item" :names ("tree-item") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Created by tree creation/traversal/selection APIs; EQ identity stable while native token is live. Retained views/snapshots can become invalid after subtree/owner deletion. Tokens are not raw native IDs." :position 311686)
("api/tree-item-alive-p" :names ("tree-item-alive-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Checks registry/owner, stronger than native IsOk non-null test. Active session required; stale views never revive on native address reuse." :position 313307)
("api/tree-item-children" :names ("tree-item-children") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Iterate native first-child/next-sibling without exposing cookies or raw IDs." :position 314458)
("api/tree-item-expanded-p" :names ("tree-item-expanded-p" "(setf tree-item-expanded-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read actual expansion; an expansion request may have no effect for leaves." :position 315479)
("api/tree-item-parent" :names ("tree-item-parent") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native parent identity." :position 316854)
("api/tree-item-text" :names ("tree-item-text" "(setf tree-item-text)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read current native label, not historical snapshot contents." :position 317752)
("api/tree-root" :names ("tree-root") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read root identity without raw adoption." :position 318942)
("api/ui-action" :names ("ui-action") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Separate closure roots live in the session queue, not the immutable ticket. No public token accessor or direct resource constructor." :position 319832)
("api/ui-action-p" :names ("ui-action-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "May be used outside a session; does not query native liveness." :position 321235)
("api/ui-action-pending-p" :names ("ui-action-pending-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Checks native owner liveness including pending ancestor deletion; observed expiry removes queued work and releases the Lisp root." :position 321824)
("api/unbind-event" :names ("unbind-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Remove exactly one registration, including from inside itself or another callback. The current callback may finish; later deliveries cannot invoke the removed function. Releases generic callback roots. A live native binding object is retained until an active callback returns. Unbinding destroys the native user-data adapter and releases global association roots, but active dispatch frames and saved snapshots can keep the Lisp value alive." :position 323032)
("api/unlink-event-handler" :names ("unlink-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Splice the native previous/next neighbors together, then detach both source edges. Does not destroy the handler, transfer ownership or move its pending queue. Already unlinked input is harmless. This differs from SETF NIL, which detaches one edge only." :position 325009)
("api/wake-up-idle" :names ("wake-up-idle") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Wake the native idle system without pumping or invoking callbacks inline. Actual handling occurs at a later native idle opportunity, not a promised immediate time." :position 326389)
("api/window" :names ("window") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Abstract CLOS base of the bound window wrappers. Reuses its wxWindow as a borrowed wxEvtHandler; construction creates one native widget, not a second handler." :position 327270)
("api/window-event-handler" :names ("window-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native GetEventHandler through the bridge managed-stack identity map. It does not reconstruct or adopt unknown native handlers and has no SETF writer." :position 328596)
("api/window-name" :names ("window-name" "(setf window-name)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the logical window name, independent of displayed labels, text, title and native ID. Names need not be unique; Unicode, empty strings and embedded NULs are preserved." :position 329655)
("api/window-position" :names ("window-position") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query position relative to parent; frame coordinates are screen-relative." :position 331051)
("api/window-process-idle-p" :names ("window-process-idle-p" "(setf window-process-idle-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/write only the window own idle opt-in extra-style bit while preserving unrelated bits. It is not effective delivery eligibility, ancestor visibility, global mode or a command to run idle callbacks." :position 331966)
("api/window-size" :names ("window-size") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query outer window dimensions in wxWidgets coordinates." :position 333450)
("api/with-application" :names ("with-application") :kind :macro :kind-name "Macro" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Evaluate BODY within CALL-WITH-APPLICATION with guaranteed cleanup." :position 334322)
("api/with-repl-application" :names ("with-repl-application") :kind :macro :kind-name "Macro" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Run setup, then evaluate terminal input while polling GUI events. STOP or EOF exits; incomplete input and debugging pause GUI events." :position 335106)
